 lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-2,\\,y<2.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-2<y<2.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=2$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n-2<y\\le 2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<y\\le 2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4a6c92f8b248cad26c90bde9b2c5481f29cb1e765b1079353614df07ba7c970"} {"question" "q-181690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c96b83962fa33f4d452d615b872bc0b214fd830aeea0ad5fbf859068e97ba2fb"} {"question" "q-181690" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4a6c92f8b248cad26c90bde9b2c5481f29cb1e765b1079353614df07ba7c970"} {"question" "q-181690" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "C"] ["math" "N"] ["math" "R"] ["math" "{C}^{2}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4a6c92f8b248cad26c90bde9b2c5481f29cb1e765b1079353614df07ba7c970"} {"question" "q-181690" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{