2c5481f29cb1e765b1079353614df07ba7c970"} {"question" "q-181690" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4a6c92f8b248cad26c90bde9b2c5481f29cb1e765b1079353614df07ba7c970"} {"question" "q-181692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/assets/7021cfd590d7e090128061d42c140ab81633f20e8cd1bff60f6252bc8e9aa882.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,-{y}^{2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4a6c92f8b248cad26c90bde9b2c5481f29cb1e765b1079353614df07ba7c970"} {"question" "q-181692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The points in our set include all those that lie *to the right* of the curve $x=-{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx>-{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $x=-{y}^{2}$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\ge -{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge -{y}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4a6c92f8b248cad26c90bde9b2c5481f29cb1e765b1079353614df07ba7c970"} {"question" "q-181692" 